# Direct development dependencies — what tests and CI need. Edit this file,
# not requirements-dev.txt.
#
# Regenerate the lockfile with:
#     .venv/bin/pip-compile requirements-dev.in
#
# Never installed into the runtime image; the Dockerfile installs only
# requirements.txt.

-c requirements.txt   # never resolve a shared dependency to a version prod does not use

pytest
ruff==0.15.9   # pinned exactly, and CI reads this pin from the lockfile rather
               # than hardcoding it a second time

# Deliberately not listed:
#
#   jupyter   — a personal tool for the notebooks, which are gitignored learning
#               notes. CI never runs them, and locking it here would add ~60
#               packages to every CI install. Install locally when needed:
#                   .venv/bin/pip install jupyter
#
#   pip-tools — it is the tool that generates these lockfiles, so locking it
#               with itself is circular. Install directly:
#                   .venv/bin/pip install pip-tools
